     "number": "1.1",
     "heading": {
      "original": {
       "kind": "heading",
       "text": "1.1 Background and Motivation",
       "level": 3,
       "number": "1.1",
       "name": "Background and Motivation"
      },
      "everyone": {
       "kind": "heading",
       "text": "1.1 Background and Motivation",
       "level": 3,
       "number": "1.1",
       "name": "Background and Motivation"
      }
     },
     "blocks": [
      {
       "original": {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Every act of perception is a meeting. Somewhere, an event occurs; energy is released; patterns of field disturbance depart the event and travel across space; they encounter matter — including the sensitive machinery of a living eye; and at the end of that journey, a mind finds itself standing inside a *scene*. The felt present — the \"now\" in which we live — is not delivered to us wholesale. It is assembled.",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "Every act of perception is a meeting. Somewhere, an event occurs; energy is released; patterns of field disturbance depart the event and travel across space; they encounter matter — including the sensitive machinery of a living eye; and at the end of that journey, a mind finds itself standing inside a *scene*. The felt present — the \"now\" in which we live — is not delivered to us wholesale. It is assembled."
       },
       "everyone": {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "Every time you open your eyes, you're at a meeting between the world and you. Somewhere out there, something happens — a leaf falls, a bulb lights, a friend smiles. That event sends out ripples of light. The ripples travel across space, they meet matter along the way, they finally hit your eye, and at the end of that journey one inside your head stands *inside a scene*. The \"now\" you live in isn't delivered to you ready-made. Your brain assembles it.",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "Every time you open your eyes, you're at a meeting between the world and you. Somewhere out there, something happens — a leaf falls, a bulb lights, a friend smiles. That event sends out ripples of light. The ripples travel across space, they meet matter along the way, they finally hit your eye, and at the end of that journey one inside your head stands *inside a scene*. The \"now\" you live in isn't delivered to you ready-made. Your brain assembles it."
       }
      },
      {
       "original": {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The central intuition of this thesis is simple enough to state in one line:",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "The central intuition of this thesis is simple enough to state in one line:"
       },
       "everyone": {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The heart of this theory fits in one line:",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "The heart of this theory fits in one line:"
       }
      },
      {
       "original": {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "A spark becomes a messenger: light brings events to our senses, and our brain weaves those messages into the felt flow of time.",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "A spark becomes a messenger: light brings events to our senses, and our brain weaves those messages into the felt flow of time."
       },
       "everyone": {
        "kind": "quote",
        "text": "A spark becomes a messenger: light brings events to our senses, and our brain weaves those messages into the felt flow of time.",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "A spark becomes a messenger: light brings events to our senses, and our brain weaves those messages into the felt flow of time."
       }
      },
      {
       "original": {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "The project is to take that intuition seriously, to state it precisely enough that it can be examined, and to defend a strong version of it as a metaphysical theory of reality.",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "The project is to take that intuition seriously, to state it precisely enough that it can be examined, and to defend a strong version of it as a metaphysical theory of reality."
       },
       "everyone": {
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "text": "That's it. The whole project is taking that one beautiful sentence seriously — saying it precisely enough to test pieces of it, and defending the strong version of it as a theory of what reality is.",
        "level": null,
        "number": null,
        "name": "That's it. The whole project is taking that one beautiful sentence seriously — saying it precisely enough to test pieces of it, and defending the strong version of it as a theory of what reality is."
       }
      }
     ]
